Subject: [PATCH] instance: do not kill the hostagent when Start's context ends

StartWithPaths starts the hostagent with exec.CommandContext(ctx, ...).
The hostagent is meant to outlive the call ("leave the hostagent process
running" when Start returns), but os/exec kills it as soon as ctx is
done, also long after Start returned.

limactl does not show it: its process exits right after Start, before
anything cancels the context, and a Ctrl-C kills limactl without
cancelling it. A Go program that uses pkg/instance does: it cancels the
context it passed (a deferred cancel, a signal handler, a request scope)
while it keeps running, and the hostagent is killed then. When the
cancel comes just before the program exits, os/exec's watcher races the
exit: the instance breaks sometimes, depending on the machine.

What follows depends on the driver:

- qemu: QEMU is a child of the hostagent, not killed with it. It keeps
  running, reparented to init, unreachable (no hostagent, so no SSH
  forward or usernet), and holds the lock on its PID file. The instance
  is Broken: "qemu driver is running but host agent is not". The next
  start fails: QEMU exits at once ("cannot create PID file: Cannot lock
  pid file"), the QEMU driver panics (below), and limactl reports "host
  agent process has exited: exit status 2". `limactl stop -f` recovers.
- vz: the VM runs in the hostagent, so it is killed with it, without a
  shutdown (not tested).

Reproduce, from a Go program, on Linux with the qemu driver:

    ctx, cancel := context.WithCancel(context.Background())
    err := instance.Start(ctx, inst, false, false) // nil, instance Running
    cancel()
    time.Sleep(time.Second)
    // store.Inspect: Broken; `ps -o ppid= -C qemu-system-x86_64`: 1

Found in agent-vm, which embeds Lima: on Linux hosts its VMs became
Broken a few seconds to minutes after a start, when the command that
started them ended (closed terminal, SIGTERM, or a plain exit losing the
race). Tested there: with this patch the VM stays Running after the
starting program ends, cancelled context included, and the next start
works.

The fix: exec.Command. ctx still bounds the wait for the hostagent to
come up (waitHostAgentStart, watchHostAgentEvents). A start cancelled
during that wait leaves the hostagent running, as an interrupted limactl
start does (the hostagent has its own process group,
BackgroundSysProcAttr, and the terminal's Ctrl-C does not reach it).

No unit test: Lima's unit tests never start a hostagent. agent-vm's e2e
test (internal/cli/e2e_test.go) fails without it.

Separate bug, to report on its own: the panic of the QEMU driver,
"panic: send on closed channel" in LimaQemuDriver.Start.func5
(pkg/driver/qemu/qemu_driver.go). When QEMU exits early, the goroutine
waiting on it closes qWaitCh and cancels the driver's context; the
ConfigureDriver goroutine then fails on that context and sends its
error on the closed qWaitCh. Already seen in #4645 (closed on its
Colima-specific part, the panic itself left unfixed). Sending with a
select on a done channel, or one closer for both goroutines, fixes it.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/pkg/instance/start.go b/pkg/instance/start.go
--- a/pkg/instance/start.go
+++ b/pkg/instance/start.go
@@ -291,7 +291,9 @@
 			args = append(args, "--progress")
 		}
 		args = append(args, inst.Name)
-		haCmd = exec.CommandContext(ctx, limactl, args...)
+		// Not exec.CommandContext: the hostagent outlives this call, and os/exec
+		// would kill it whenever ctx ends, even after Start returned.
+		haCmd = exec.Command(limactl, args...)

 		haCmd.SysProcAttr = executil.BackgroundSysProcAttr

